From 2dc4fd1be7a996d7eeff06983845a8fd95ce6f9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:01:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Safety rails on load + durable run state (groundwork for
 autonomy)

Safety (perfagent/safety.py, enforced in the runner):
- target allow-list (static scan of script URLs + runtime guard on hosts hit)
- max users / max duration read from the script via 'k6 inspect' (fail closed)
- concurrency cap, duration watchdog
- durable kill switch: stops live runs, refuses new ones; API + top-bar control
- pre-flight respects the allow-list; blocks and safety stops are audited

Durable runs (runner/store.py, 'runs' table):
- run state saved on start, every heartbeat, and on finish
- get_run falls back to the DB: finished runs + reports survive a restart
- runs orphaned by a restart are marked 'interrupted'; leftover k6 is stopped
- /api/runs/active + UI banner to rejoin a live run after a refresh
- stop works across processes (stop_requested)

Verdict: a run cut short (stopped/interrupted) is never PASS -> inconclusive.
Report waits for final metrics; response includes the final snapshot.
deps: psutil. 35 new tests.
